before:
The supplied HTML is separate from the CSS.

```html
<button class="tile" type="button">A small state change</button>
```

```css
.tile { opacity: 1; transition: opacity 0.08s linear; }
.tile.muted { opacity: 0.4; }
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .tile { transition-duration: 0s; } }
```

after:
This rule fades only the opacity. `0.08s` is the time in seconds. `linear` means a steady speed.
```css
.tile {
  opacity: 1;
  transition: opacity 0.08s linear;
}
.tile.muted {
  opacity: 0.4;
}
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .tile { transition-duration: 0s; }
}
```
